WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.539 --> 00:00:06.460
There is something really interesting going
on in the still early stages of the 2020 general

00:00:06.460 --> 00:00:07.460
election.

00:00:07.460 --> 00:00:11.570
Now I'm saying general election because the
Democratic primary, I guess we can say is

00:00:11.570 --> 00:00:12.960
well underway now.

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:17.780
Debates start in just a couple of weeks, but
on the general election side, Donald Trump

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:22.230
is only now starting to even really campaign
in earnest.

00:00:22.230 --> 00:00:27.870
You might remember that he filed for reelection,
I think it was on inauguration day in 2017

00:00:27.870 --> 00:00:32.540
or soon thereafter, or right before, right
around inauguration day 2017.

00:00:32.540 --> 00:00:36.950
Trump was technically speaking, running for
reelection in 2020.

00:00:36.950 --> 00:00:40.370
But he's not really fully started his campaign.

00:00:40.370 --> 00:00:45.850
And it turns out the Trump campaign in the
last several weeks has taken some internal

00:00:45.850 --> 00:00:52.640
polls of key battleground states and Donald
Trump is losing badly in some of those.

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:56.239
And we've now learned thanks to a really good
New York Times report that Donald Trump has

00:00:56.239 --> 00:01:02.480
been going out of his way to demand that his
staffers and his administration suppress the,

00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:05.780
uh, negative internal polls that they have
taken.

00:01:05.780 --> 00:01:11.170
For example, internal polls in Michigan and
Pennsylvania show that Donald Trump is currently

00:01:11.170 --> 00:01:17.670
losing badly against any of the hypothetical
Democratic presidential nominees.

00:01:17.670 --> 00:01:22.640
Important to understand, these are internal
campaign polls.

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:24.070
They're not public polls.

00:01:24.070 --> 00:01:27.890
There are polls that the campaign takes for
their own purposes.

00:01:27.890 --> 00:01:33.840
Trump's campaign went and did polling in 17
states, and when Donald Trump was presented

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:36.929
with the information, he said, no, no, no.

00:01:36.929 --> 00:01:39.960
Say that we're doing well and bury this data.

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:41.869
We don't want this stuff getting out.

00:01:41.869 --> 00:01:47.940
Now, unfortunately, even without the incipient
leaks from the Trump administration, other

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:53.830
pollsters have also been polling in many of
these states, and that information is now

00:01:53.830 --> 00:01:59.090
public morning consult, for example, found
that registered voters in a bunch of states

00:01:59.090 --> 00:02:01.270
are really negative on Donald Trump.

00:02:01.270 --> 00:02:04.480
Only 39% of New Hampshire voters approve of
Trump.

00:02:04.480 --> 00:02:08.459
Only 42% of Wisconsin voters approve of Trump.

00:02:08.459 --> 00:02:13.250
Trump has a minus 13 unfavorability versus
favoribility rating.

00:02:13.250 --> 00:02:20.180
Remember, Trump won Wisconsin narrowly in
2016, Michigan, which Trump won in 2016 he's

00:02:20.180 --> 00:02:27.540
minus 12 in terms of approval, Iowa, which
Trump won in 2016 he's minus 12 unfavorability,

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:29.370
Pennsylvania minus seven.

00:02:29.370 --> 00:02:36.719
He won that in 2016, Arizona Trump is now
minus six, which he won in 2016, Ohio and

00:02:36.719 --> 00:02:39.109
North Carolina, Trump won both.

00:02:39.109 --> 00:02:41.129
He's minus four right now.

00:02:41.129 --> 00:02:49.559
And even if you look incredibly at some solidly
red states that Trump won in 2016, it's shaky

00:02:49.559 --> 00:02:50.689
in Georgia.

00:02:50.689 --> 00:02:51.999
Trump is only plus one.

00:02:51.999 --> 00:02:54.480
Uh, in North Dakota and Kansas.

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:57.930
Uh, Trump has only plus one Texas and Indiana.

00:02:57.930 --> 00:03:00.930
Trump is only plus three in net favor ability.

00:03:00.930 --> 00:03:06.489
Now I, before I go any further, this tells
us nothing about how 2020 will go.

00:03:06.489 --> 00:03:07.489
Okay.

00:03:07.489 --> 00:03:11.219
This doesn't mean no matter where you vote,
that you don't have to worry about voting

00:03:11.219 --> 00:03:12.760
for someone other than Donald Trump.

00:03:12.760 --> 00:03:18.139
But these numbers combined with Trump panicking
and trying to suppress news of these PR of

00:03:18.139 --> 00:03:23.049
this polling does tell us that number one,
Trump is at least somewhat worried.

00:03:23.049 --> 00:03:29.519
Uh, number two, Trump knows that to some degree
things are not looking great in some of these

00:03:29.519 --> 00:03:30.519
key states.

00:03:30.519 --> 00:03:37.620
And number three, this tells us Trump can
easily be removed in 2020 if voter turnout

00:03:37.620 --> 00:03:42.189
is what it should be, what could be what we
want it to be.

00:03:42.189 --> 00:03:47.639
In one sense though, I think it's good that
Donald Trump is reacting this way to negative

00:03:47.639 --> 00:03:48.639
polls.

00:03:48.639 --> 00:03:55.639
If Trump's side negative Paul's and said,
I need to turn on my campaign game 100%, um,

00:03:55.639 --> 00:03:58.540
that's actually something he could do to turn
these numbers around.

00:03:58.540 --> 00:04:04.159
If Trump sees these numbers and says, let's
suppress them rather than let me campaign

00:04:04.159 --> 00:04:05.450
really hard.

00:04:05.450 --> 00:04:11.230
Hopefully he just hangs out, plays golf, watches
Fox News, ignores the polling, ignores the

00:04:11.230 --> 00:04:16.190
dissatisfaction from the country tweets nonsense,
and that'll help them be defeated.

00:04:16.190 --> 00:04:22.310
But as Trump's opposition, it's really important
that we not be in any way satisfied just by

00:04:22.310 --> 00:04:26.790
seeing this data into thinking that this is
going to be an easy one in 2020 by any means

00:04:26.790 --> 00:04:33.210
in every state, every voter should be behaving
as if your vote could be the vote that hands

00:04:33.210 --> 00:04:37.250
your state, either to Donald Trump or to somebody
else.

00:04:37.250 --> 00:04:40.980
By virtue of whether you choose to vote or
choose to stay home, we don't know which states

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:42.980
are going to ultimately make the difference.

00:04:42.980 --> 00:04:45.900
It could once again be places like Michigan
and Wisconsin.

00:04:45.900 --> 00:04:47.250
It could be somewhere else.

00:04:47.250 --> 00:04:49.440
The polling is interesting.

00:04:49.440 --> 00:04:54.680
Trump's internal team finding that he's losing
bigly in some of these states is fascinating,

00:04:54.680 --> 00:04:59.880
but none of it should be used as a reason
to do anything other than vote in the primary

00:04:59.880 --> 00:05:03.060
vote in November of 2020 period.

